WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.950
- Sana-chan, keep well -

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.910
This is the present from me.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.830
That's really cool.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.140
Aoi-chan, did you make this?

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:16.220
Yeah. But mum helped me with the difficult bits.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.530
It's a bit crooked over here though.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.930
While I was squeezing out the white chocolate...

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:29.880
...I was thinking about Sana-chan moving soon, and how we won't see each other anymore...

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.160
...so I became teary and made a mistake there.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:35.920
Sana!

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.480
This is the present from me.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.590
What's that? That's weird.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:44.440
It's not weird. It's a lure.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.200
Oh, the ones you use for fishing, right?

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.050
You've been doing that a lot lately.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.650
I made it myself. 
It's incredibly well done.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.780
It's weird.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.320
Well, what did you make, sis?

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.020
This is mine.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.410
What's that? That's terrible!

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.240
And only one side?

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.660
What can I do? I tried my best but I couldn't finish it in time.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.580
I'm sorry, Sana. This was all I could do.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.250
Not at all.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.530
Nanaka-chan, what's your present?

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:23.620
Well, this is what I made.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.410
Actually...

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.350
...I made a song for Sana-chan.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.840
Well, I didn't really compose it or anything.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:37.090
But my violin teacher taught me a lot of things.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:41.260
I only managed to learn about half, though.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.580
Will you listen to it?

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.050
Sure.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:54.390
Here goes nothing.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.690
I only learnt that much.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:42.150
I'll definitely finish it by the next time we meet.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.030
So please wait.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.420
Did I fall asleep?

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:40.860
Sana!

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:50.760
Come to think of it, what did Shuu say back then?

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:54.100
The train was too noisy then, so I couldn't hear anything.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:02.660
The Place of Memories

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.050
<i>Has it been five years?</i>

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:22.060
<i>Surprisingly, it still looks the same.</i>

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:25.300
<i>I guess the place wouldn't change much within five years.</i>

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.600
<i>I remember this being...</i>

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.390
<i>And wasn't there a bento shop over here?</i>

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.440
<i>I see.</i>

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.670
<i>I guess some things have changed.</i>

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.070
I guess I can take a little detour.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.780
<i>The sakuras here really don't bloom.</i>

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:26.050
<i>This sure brings back memories.</i>

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:31.630
<i>I had a lot of fun with everyone over here.</i>

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:41.610
<i>Oh, yeah. I gave that to Nanaka during the festival.</i>

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:57.290
I'm giving this to you.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:03.960
I won this at a throwing game earlier.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:06.520
I don't want it, so I'm giving it to you.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.580
Can I really have it?

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.410
Sana-chan, thanks!

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:17.410
Just so you know, I'm only giving it to you because I don't want it.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.800
She sure was pretty though.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:00.310
How may I help?

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.420
No, I mean...

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:05.090
I'd like a written fortune please.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.900
That'll be 100 yen.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:23.040
- Misfortune -

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:23.620
Misfortune, huh?

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.550
Furthermore, there will be relationship problems with girls.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.640
<i>Hello, who's there?</i>

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:51.150
This is Hidaka. I'm here for my room key.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.220
<i>Sana-chan, is that you?</i>

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.380
Yeah.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:58.680
<i>Oh, please wait, I'll open the door soon.</i>

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.430
Sana-chan?

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.430
It's really you, Sana-chan!

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:11.040
It's been so long. The real thing.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:14.210
I really missed you.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:14.210
-Don't tell me, you're...

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:15.760
...Aoi-chan?

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:22.940
That's right. It's Aoi.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:26.330
Sana-chan.

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:30.860
Don't tell me you forgot me?

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.840
No, I didn't forget.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:35.810
It's just... how do I put it?

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:40.340
I just kinda mistook you for another person.

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:44.200
Is it because of this?

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.520
My eyesight deteriorated after I entered high school.

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:52.720
So, I had to wear glasses.
 But, it doesn't look good, does it?

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.500
Not at all. The glasses look really good on you.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.680
Really?

00:08:58.460 --> 00:08:59.690
Of course.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.120
Thank goodness.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.520
But, what did you mean by mistaking me for someone else?

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:08.810
Well...

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.710
Forgive us. We're the land-owners.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:20.350
My mum was supposed to meet you, but she's out right now.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:24.380
Please.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:29.840
The movers brought in all your belongings this morning.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:32.920
Is the desk okay over there?

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.530
Yeah, that's fine.

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:39.110
If you like, I can help you with the unpacking.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:42.580
Oh, yeah. That's right.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:44.710
It'd be a great help.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.640
Actually, I'll be fine on my own.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:53.060
But unpacking by yourself will be tough, won't it?

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:59.030
It's fine. It's not much, so I'll be able to finish real quick.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:01.490
Really?

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:03.730
Well then, here's the key.

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:05.960
I leave the spare with you, okay?

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:09.470
I'll be going back now.

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:12.530
However, if you run into any problems, feel free to call me.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:14.580
Got it. Thanks.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:15.590
See ya.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:41.260
This should be enough for the moment.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:54.130
<i>Oh, yeah. Aoi-chan often read at the bookstore for free.</i>

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:57.050
You can't have both.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.830
Please pick one.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:01.070
Why?

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:04.760
I'll read it here if you don't buy them.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.680
<i>Kusaka Sanzo Ichioshi.</i>

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:13.520
<i>This year's best seller.</i>

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.880
<i>It's only April. The season is starting early.</i>

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:20.890
Sana-chan?

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:23.890
You're gonna buy that book?

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:25.490
No...

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:27.900
I just thought that it was kinda interesting.

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:30.060
It's a true masterpiece!

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:32.320
I really recommend it.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:34.350
Oh, really?

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:40.670
The retired magician solving the mystery with the help of a cop friend.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:43.820
It's also called a detective story filled with mysteries.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:49.140
Firstly, the detective character who was a former magician is really cool.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:53.630
And then, he receives no leads, and the situation looks dire.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:59.230
Each and every time he manages to solve the case by himself, even without any hints.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:03.480
A hidden room. A murder case with uncertainties and no suspects. Many messages.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:07.620
Everyone takes their respective paths and have their own short story.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:12.410
They're all good. But the very last one was amazing.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:15.470
And at the very last second of the complicated mystery...

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:19.550
The spoilers come here, so please cover your ears.

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:38.860
So, is it okay now?

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:44.200
Sorry, I get carried away when it comes to books.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.530
It's okay.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.750
You didn't spoil it or anything.

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:58.260
<i>Aoi-chan's passion for books hasn't changed at all.</i>

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:00.310
Oh, yeah.

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:04.420
Where's a good place to eat around here?

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:08.950
I was thinking of cooking for myself but...

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:11.280
...I figured I should just eat out today.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:15.420
Then, why don't you come over to my place?

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.210
There's lots to eat.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:29.330
You've sure grown after I took my eyes off you.

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:30.910
Not at all.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:36.530
Well, since you moved from this town like five years back...

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:37.960
...now you must be...

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.210
Sixteen.

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:40.590
I see.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.980
Aoi is a year older then.

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:46.780
You're still growing, so eat up.

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:48.030
Pardon me.

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:49.190
Thanks for the meal.

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:51.820
Oh, my. "Pardon me", he says.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:56.350
Your parents left you in our hands, so please don't be so modest.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:59.350
To us, tenant and landlord, parent and child, are one and the same.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.460
That's right, Sana-chan.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:04.760
Why don't you become my son-in-law?

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.830
So you mean, with Aoi-chan?

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:12.650
Mommy, what are you saying?

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:17.720
That's right, it's still a bit early for Aoi to get married.

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:21.430
I'm just kidding obviously.

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:24.110
Oh, so you were kidding?

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:26.350
That's right. It's just a joke.

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:29.260
How could Aoi get married?

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:35.230
Mommy had to say such weird things.

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:38.880
But...

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.320
...Sana-chan, you really came back.

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:47.180
I'm home.

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.580
I'm home, huh?

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:01.330
I really came back.

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:04.920
<i>But then again...</i>

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:10.180
<i>That Aoi-chan turned out like that.</i>

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:14.720
<i>If that were the case, then perhaps Nanaka too?</i>

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.900
Sana-chan. I missed you so much.

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:35.350
Hello?

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:37.920
Oh, mum. It's just you.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:42.860
I'll be fine.

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:44.800
At Aoi-chan's place.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:46.760
I met the landlords as well.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.200
You don't have to worry.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.400
I had my dinner as well.

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:54.550
It was at Aoi-chan's place though.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:16:00.280
Yeah, just like you told me, I've purchased the ingredients for breakfast tomorrow.

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:01.400
Yeah, I got it.

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.350
I'll be fine.

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:06.670
I'll be going to school tomorrow as well.

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:21.960
Yes, who's that?

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:24.480
Ah, Sana-chan.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:41.110
It slipped my mind because I was sleepy.

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:43.130
Me too. Sorry for being so sudden.

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:47.270
More importantly, we're gonna be late. I overslept again.

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:52.270
Since this is the first time you've stayed by yourself, I thought I should check on you.

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:57.340
Today is the opening ceremony though.
 So, it's okay to go late.

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.830
No way.

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:05.460
And I rushed over without having breakfast again.

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:10.630
<i>Aoi-chan sure doesn't know how to take things slow.</i>

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.140
That's right, Sana-chan.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.770
Since you've just gotten up, you haven't had breakfast yet, right?

00:17:14.770 --> 00:17:16.040
That's correct.

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.670
Then, I'll make some for you.

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:22.690
In return, let me have breakfast together with you.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:25.350
But then...

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:30.480
<i>Why does she have an apron?</i>

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:35.880
Let's see. Bacon, eggs and milk.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:38.320
Looks like you have all the ingredients.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.350
Sorry, I only bought enough for myself.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.400
It's okay.

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:49.530
After drinking this, it'll taste the same.

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:50.440
Right?

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:57.850
This is the staff room.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:17:59.470
Thank you for taking the trouble.

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:03.740
Sana-chan, about this morning...

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:09.370
Well, I got the time wrong and hurriedly woke you up.

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:14.350
It's really embarrassing, so please don't tell anyone.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:16.360
It's our secret, okay?

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:19.870
Sure.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:21.080
See ya.

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:30.250
Do you need something from the staff room?

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:40.390
Alright everyone. Please get back to your seats.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:49.180
I'm Fujimura Yuzuki and I'll be 2-F's homeroom teacher for the year.

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.950
I'm in charge of Science.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:55.110
But, I didn't go into Science because I'm thick-headed.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.120
So, nice to meet you all.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:04.010
Hmm, I see a few familiar faces here.

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:06.240
Then, before we start the opening ceremony...

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:11.410
...let me introduce you to the transfer student who's gonna be joining us at Sakuranomori High.

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:13.140
Please enter.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:18.140
Sana!?

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:19.180
Shuu?

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:23.270
And Shuri too?

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:26.850
You know the Wakatsuki twins?

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:32.540
It's not just <i>know</i>. Sana and I used to play a lot together when we were kids.

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:35.020
We're really close friends.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:36.510
I see.

00:19:36.510 --> 00:19:38.530
So, that means I'll have to give you special attention, right?

00:19:40.310 --> 00:19:41.490
Why?

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:47.850
<i>The cleaning for the opening ceremony will now begin.</i>

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:52.920
Well, I heard that you were coming back here...

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.580
...but, I never expected us to be in the same class.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.130
Is this the bond of our friendship?

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:04.480
But, why did you come back all of a sudden?

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.520
Well, I have my reasons.

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:11.380
Don't worry about the minor details.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:15.520
Anyway, I'm just really happy that you've come back.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:19.790
<i>That's good. Shuu and Shuri haven't changed either.</i>

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:23.720
That's nice though. I'd like to try living on my own as well.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:26.910
What are you saying? You can't even cook.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:32.490
Oh, shut up! Even I know how to put stuff into boiling water.

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:33.920
Cup noodles?

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:41.340
Weren't you the one at the temple yesterday?

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.520
So you attend this school too?

00:20:45.520 --> 00:20:48.270
It's a pleasure to meet you. 
Though this isn't the first time.

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:50.230
Since we've met at the temple yesterday.

00:20:50.670 --> 00:20:52.050
Hey, Sana.

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:53.260
That's kinda...

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:04.340
What was that...?!

00:21:15.470 --> 00:21:18.380
<i>So you mean...</i>

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.350
<i>...that was Nanaka?</i>

00:21:25.690 --> 00:21:27.890
You've really done it this time, Sana.

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:29.210
You've really done it.

00:21:29.210 --> 00:21:33.070
If I were Nanaka, I'd use my electric arm on him right there and then.

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:36.470
Or perhaps, my iron claw!

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:42.770
I'd strangle him like this!

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:47.040
I give up. You're gonna crush me!

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:50.580
Next time on Myself; Yourself:
The Important Melody

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:54.990
The Important Melody

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.150
Please look forward to it.

00:21:52.150 --> 00:21:54.720
I'm not really looking forward to it though.
